---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Postern — 6-slide overview"
  description="Six slides summarising the Postern research artifact: problem, architecture, Lean proofs, Rust mirror, open problems."
  bare={true}
>
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/reveal.js@5.1.0/dist/reveal.css"
  />
  <link
    rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/reveal.js@5.1.0/dist/theme/white.css"
    id="reveal-theme"
  />

  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="slides">

      <!-- S1: Title / thesis -->
      <section class="slide-title">
        <p class="eyebrow">Research artifact &middot; 2026</p>
        <h1>Postern</h1>
        <h2>Lean-verified Biscuit-Datalog policies for agentic data lakehouses</h2>
        <p class="claim">
          The plan rewriter is <code>sorry</code>-free in Lean
          (axioms: <code>{`{ propext, Quot.sound }`}</code>). A Rust
          mirror runs the same logic; a conformance harness keeps
          them byte-equal on a hand-curated JSON corpus. The Datalog
          evaluator is in active proof work.
        </p>
        <p class="byline">FractalBox &middot; Track 3</p>
      </section>

      <!-- S2: Problem -->
      <section>
        <h2>The collapse at ETL</h2>
        <p>
          Channel ACLs, field-level security, and customer-scoped tokens
          collapse <em>at ETL into a single ingest IAM role</em>.
        </p>
        <p>
          An indirect-prompt-injected agent inherits the
          <strong class="bad">union</strong> of upstream principals' permissions,
          not the <strong class="good">intersection</strong> under its querying
          identity.
        </p>
        <pre class="mermaid" is:raw>
flowchart LR
  classDef src fill:#fde,stroke:#a33,color:#333
  classDef etl fill:#fee,stroke:#a33,color:#333,stroke-dasharray:4
  classDef agent fill:#fec,stroke:#b15c2e,color:#333
  src1[CRM&nbsp;ACL]:::src --> etl((ingest&nbsp;IAM))
  src2[Card&nbsp;FLS]:::src  --> etl
  src3[Customer&nbsp;tokens]:::src --> etl
  etl:::etl --> lake[(lakehouse)]
  lake --> agent[LLM agent]:::agent
  agent -->|union of all sources!| out([result])
        </pre>
      </section>

      <!-- S3: Architecture (verbatim mermaid from paper §Design) -->
      <section>
        <h2>Architecture</h2>
        <p class="muted small">From paper &sect;Design.</p>
        <pre class="mermaid" is:raw>
flowchart LR
  agent[LLM agent] -->|MCP plan + biscuit| gw{{Postern gateway}}
  subgraph TCB
    gw -->|verify| bc[biscuit verifier]
    bc -->|principal| rw[Lean-extracted rewriter]
    pol[(policy)] --> rw
    cat[(catalog)] --> rw
    rw -->|Option Plan| exe[DuckDB / Polars]
  end
  exe --> agent
        </pre>
        <p class="small">
          Trust boundary contains policy + catalog + rewriter; the agent
          reaches DuckDB/Polars only through the gateway.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- S4: What Lean proves -->
      <section>
        <h2>What Lean proves</h2>
        <table class="theorems">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>theorem</th>
              <th>file</th>
              <th>status</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><code>rewrite_sound</code></td>
              <td><code>Postern.lean</code></td>
              <td><span class="badge ok">proved</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>rewrite_filter_sound</code></td>
              <td><code>Postern.lean</code></td>
              <td><span class="badge ok">proved</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>eval_monotone</code></td>
              <td><code>Datalog.lean</code></td>
              <td><span class="badge partial">proof reduces to one sorry</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>eval_sound</code></td>
              <td><code>Datalog.lean</code></td>
              <td><span class="badge todo">stated, sorry</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><code>eval_terminates</code></td>
              <td><code>Datalog.lean</code></td>
              <td><span class="badge todo">stated, sorry</span></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="small">
          Axioms of proven theorems:
          <code>{`{ propext, Quot.sound }`}</code>.
          <code>eval_monotone</code>'s body is written but reduces
          to <code>herbrandBound_mono</code> — a labelled
          <code>sorry</code> we expose rather than hide. Eight
          supporting iterator lemmas are proven.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- S5: What Rust does -->
      <section>
        <h2>What Rust does</h2>
        <p>
          <code>postern-core</code> mirrors the Lean rewriter one-for-one.
          The gateway plan is for it to call
          <code>biscuit_auth::datalog::World</code> for evaluation —
          <strong>that migration is task #4, not yet in this artifact.</strong>
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>postern-core</code> — Plan IR, policy, <code>rewrite()</code>.</li>
          <li><code>postern-guardrail</code> — branded <code>Cap&lt;'sc, C&gt;</code> + opaque-receipt sinks.</li>
          <li><code>postern-diff</code> — diff-tests Lean reference ↔ Rust output on a JSON corpus (18/18 cases: 15 accept, 3 refuse).</li>
          <li><code>postern-wasm</code> — surface this site loads.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="small">
          The WASM module powering the <a href="/demo">demo</a> is today the
          column-grant DSL evaluator; Biscuit-Datalog migration in progress.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- S6: Open problems -->
      <section>
        <h2>Open problems</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Block <strong>attenuation</strong> — biscuit blocks can shrink rights mid-flight; the rewriter doesn't yet model this.</li>
          <li><strong>Audience checks</strong> + <strong>expiry</strong> — bind tokens to gateway identity and a time window.</li>
          <li><strong>Key rotation</strong> for the verifier without invalidating in-flight tokens.</li>
          <li><strong>Cross-relation joins</strong> — the current IR is single-relation; multi-relation grants compose non-trivially.</li>
          <li><strong>Aggregation with a DP boundary</strong> — summary outputs without leaking row-level columns.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="muted small">Paper &sect;6 enumerates the full open-problem list.</p>
        <p class="ribbon">
          <a href="/paper">Read the paper</a> &middot;
          <a href="/demo">Try the WASM demo</a> &middot;
          <a href="https://github.com/debuggingfuture/secure-program-synthesis">GitHub</a>
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </div>

  <script>
    import Reveal from "reveal.js";
    import mermaid from "mermaid";

    mermaid.initialize({
      startOnLoad: false,
      theme: "neutral",
      securityLevel: "strict",
      flowchart: { curve: "linear", htmlLabels: true },
      fontFamily: "ui-monospace, JetBrains Mono, Menlo, monospace",
    });

    // Render mermaid blocks on each slide as it becomes active.
    async function renderMermaidInSlide(slide: Element | null) {
      if (!slide) return;
      const pres = slide.querySelectorAll("pre.mermaid:not([data-rendered])");
      for (const pre of Array.from(pres)) {
        const el = pre as HTMLElement;
        el.setAttribute("data-rendered", "1");
        const src = el.textContent ?? "";
        const id = "mmd-" + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2);
        try {
          const { svg } = await mermaid.render(id, src);
          el.innerHTML = svg;
        } catch (e) {
          el.innerHTML = `<pre style="color:#b03a3a">mermaid error: ${String(e)}</pre>`;
        }
      }
    }

    const deck = new Reveal({
      hash: true,
      slideNumber: "c/t",
      controlsTutorial: false,
      transition: "fade",
      width: 1120,
      height: 720,
      margin: 0.04,
    });
    deck.initialize().then(() => {
      renderMermaidInSlide(deck.getCurrentSlide());
      // reveal.js's `on()` lacks types for its custom events in
      // @types/reveal.js, so we cast through the wider Element form.
      (deck as unknown as {
        on: (
          ev: string,
          h: (e: { currentSlide: Element }) => void,
        ) => void;
      }).on("slidechanged", (e) => renderMermaidInSlide(e.currentSlide));
    });
  </script>

  <style is:global>
    /* Override reveal.js defaults to match site voice. */
    .reveal {
      font-family: var(--font-sans, system-ui, sans-serif);
      color: #222;
    }

    .reveal h1,
    .reveal h2,
    .reveal h3 {
      font-family: ui-serif, "Iowan Old Style", Palatino, serif;
      text-transform: none;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: #1a1a1a;
    }

    .reveal h1 {
      font-size: 3rem;
      margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    }

    .reveal h2 {
      font-size: 1.7rem;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid #d9d6cf;
      padding-bottom: 0.3rem;
    }

    .reveal code {
      font-family: ui-monospace, "JetBrains Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.88em;
      background: #f2efe7;
      padding: 0.05rem 0.3rem;
      border-radius: 2px;
    }

    .reveal pre.mermaid {
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid #d9d6cf;
      padding: 1rem;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      max-width: 95%;
      margin: 0.6rem auto;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .reveal pre.mermaid svg {
      max-width: 100% !important;
      height: auto !important;
    }

    .reveal .slide-title {
      text-align: left;
    }

    .reveal .eyebrow {
      font-family: ui-monospace, "JetBrains Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 0.74rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      color: #b15c2e;
    }

    .reveal .slide-title h2 {
      border: none;
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: 400;
      color: #555;
      font-size: 1.4rem;
      margin-top: 0.5rem;
    }

    .reveal .claim {
      max-width: 28em;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      margin: 1.6rem 0 0;
      color: #333;
    }

    .reveal .byline {
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 1.5rem;
      left: 0;
      font-family: ui-monospace, "JetBrains Mono", Menlo, monospace;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: #888;
    }

    .reveal .muted {
      color: #888;
    }

    .reveal .small {
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      color: #555;
    }

    .reveal .bad {
      color: #b03a3a;
    }

    .reveal .good {
      color: #2f6b3a;
    }

    .reveal ul {
      font-size: 0.96rem;
    }

    .reveal .theorems {
      width: 100%;
      font-size: 0.86rem;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin: 0.6rem 0;
    }

    .reveal .theorems th,
    .reveal .theorems td {
      border-bottom: 1px solid #e3e0d8;
      padding: 0.4rem 0.6rem;
      text-align: left;
    }

    .reveal .badge {
      font-family: ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
      border-radius: 2px;
    }

    .reveal .badge.ok {
      background: rgba(47, 107, 58, 0.12);
      color: #2f6b3a;
    }

    .reveal .badge.todo {
      background: #fff7e6;
      color: #b88330;
    }

    .reveal .badge.partial {
      background: rgba(177, 92, 46, 0.14);
      color: #b15c2e;
    }

    .reveal .ribbon {
      margin-top: 1.4rem;
      font-size: 0.94rem;
    }

    .reveal a {
      color: #b15c2e;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
